---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocumentationNav from '../components/DocumentationNav.astro';
import PageBreadcrumb from '../components/shell/PageBreadcrumb.astro';
import { seoPolicy } from '../data/seo';
const sections = [
  { id: 'people', label: 'People and content' },
  { id: 'signals', label: 'Technical signals' },
  { id: 'ai-search', label: 'AI discovery and reuse' },
  { id: 'experience', label: 'Experience and evidence' },
  { id: 'lifecycle', label: 'Ownership and release' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="SEO policy"
  description="GenUX SEO policy: useful factual content, consistent metadata, crawlable documentation, AI discovery and verified release evidence."
  slug="seo-policy"
>
  <PageBreadcrumb
    items={[
      { label: 'Overview', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Project', href: '/project/' },
    ]}
    current="SEO policy"
  />
  <h1>SEO policy</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Help people find, understand and use GenUX. Search engines and AI discovery receive the same
    factual, accessible documentation that people read.
  </p>
  <DocumentationNav items={sections} />
  <section id="people" data-doc-section="people" aria-labelledby="people-title">
    <h2 id="people-title">People and content</h2>
    <p>
      Every document serves one real task. Start with a clear answer, then explain purpose, usage,
      limitations, accessibility and sources. Keep essential text and links in server-rendered HTML.
    </p>
    <p>
      Component examples, API mappings and source references must describe the implementation that
      exists. Recorded demonstrations are labelled; a local fixture is not a live model or server
      integration.
    </p>
    <p>
      Editors review correctness and usefulness. A static check cannot certify either. Do not
      fabricate authors, review dates, reviews, prices, benchmarks or citations; do not create
      keyword-stuffed or near-identical pages solely for search traffic.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="signals" data-doc-section="signals" aria-labelledby="signals-title">
    <h2 id="signals-title">Technical signals</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/url-policy/">URL policy</a> owns stable addresses, canonical URLs, directories,
      aliases, sitemap and real 404 behavior. Each canonical document has one descriptive title and
      summary, consistent sharing metadata, explicit indexing directives and the correct source
      language.
    </p>
    <p>
      Structured data describes actual pages: directories as CollectionPage, technical references as
      TechArticle, and general pages as WebPage. The project graph points to the actual public
      source and existing license. It does not invent ratings, offers or a search action.
    </p>
    <p>
      The shared social image is a branded fallback. Editorial images should be relevant and have
      alternatives and intrinsic dimensions. Display controls and navigation are not the main answer
      to a search query.
    </p>
    <p>
      English is the server-rendered canonical language. Turkish display translation shares its URL.
      Separate language addresses require actual translated HTML and reciprocal language links.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="ai-search" data-doc-section="ai-search" aria-labelledby="ai-search-title">
    <h2 id="ai-search-title">AI discovery and reuse</h2>
    <p>
      Use clear definitions, direct answers, meaningful headings and verifiable references. Machine
      indexes point to canonical HTML; there is no special AI schema, text file or ranking
      guarantee.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/llms.txt">Text discovery index</a> and <a href="/url-manifest.json">URL manifest</a>{' '}
      are conveniences. Search-crawler access and model-training permissions are separate decisions.
      Existing training permissions remain unchanged.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not serve hidden instructions or different factual content to crawlers. Google Search,
      Google-Extended, OAI-SearchBot and GPTBot have distinct purposes; a project-path robots file
      cannot govern the host.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="experience" data-doc-section="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-title">
    <h2 id="experience-title">Experience and evidence</h2>
    <p>
      Preserve readable Outfit typography, user zoom, keyboard focus, 320 CSS px access, image
      stability and conditional asset delivery. Static SEO adds no client JavaScript or tracking
      scripts.
    </p>
    <p>
      Real-user targets at the 75th percentile, measured separately for mobile and desktop: LCP ≤{' '}
      {seoPolicy.experienceTargets.lcpMs / 1000}s, INP ≤ {seoPolicy.experienceTargets.inpMs}ms and
      CLS ≤ {seoPolicy.experienceTargets.cls}. A local build or screenshot does not prove these
      metrics.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <a href="/seo-report.json">build SEO report</a> records static checks and states which
      evidence was not measured. Search indexing, AI citations and field performance remain
      unverified until actually observed.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="lifecycle" data-doc-section="lifecycle" aria-labelledby="lifecycle-title">
    <h2 id="lifecycle-title">Ownership and release</h2>
    <p>
      Shared metadata and schema come from one SEO model. The final artifact gate rejects missing or
      inconsistent signals, unsupported claims and a broken social image. The source{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/atonota/genux/blob/main/docs/SEO-POLICY.md">SEO policy</a> defines
      maintainer and editorial responsibilities.
    </p>
    <p>
      GitHub project Pages owns /genux/, not host-root robots, other repositories, Search Console or
      response-header configuration. These require their actual host/property control. This policy
      installs no analytics, paid services or scheduled monitoring.
    </p>
    <p>
      Keep local validation, commit, CI, live publication and search-engine results separate. Review
      factual content when the product or its references change; never manufacture automatic
      freshness.
    </p>
    <p>
      References:{' '}
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ai-features">
        Google AI features
      </a>
      ,{' '}
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/sd-policies">
        structured-data policies
      </a>
      , <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/bots">OpenAI crawlers</a> and{' '}
      <a href="https://web.dev/articles/vitals">Web Vitals</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
